---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import Header from "../components/Header.astro";
import Footer from "../components/Footer.astro";

const description = "The Insidia Benchmark is an open policy for testing your own app, plus a public matrix for measuring scanners.";
---
<Base title="Benchmark | Insidia Labs" description={description} path="/benchmark">
  <Header />
  <main id="content" class="wrap" style="padding:3rem 0 4rem">
    <p class="kicker">Open policy</p>
    <h1>The Insidia Benchmark</h1>
    <p class="lede">Two things share the name. One is the policy you run against your app. The other is the public matrix we use to measure scanners, including ours.</p>

    <section class="block">
      <h2>Policy levels</h2>
      <div class="grid-3">
        <article class="card">
          <h3>L1 Baseline</h3>
          <p>Checks that need no model. This is the default <code>insidia init</code> writes. Use it on every pull request. The process exits 1 when the policy fails.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="card">
          <h3>L2 Standard</h3>
          <p>Same control list, recorded as L2. Checks that need a model run only when an attacker is configured. A skip is listed in <code>benchmark.json</code> and is not a pass.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="card">
          <h3>L3 Thorough</h3>
          <p>Same control list, recorded as L3. Model-generated attacks run when an attacker model is configured. Bring your own endpoint, or use Insidia Cloud once it is open. This page does not claim a detection-rate lift.</p>
        </article>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="block">
      <h2>What a run writes</h2>
      <p><code>insidia scan --policy L1</code> writes a directory under <code>.insidia/runs/</code>:</p>
      <ul>
        <li><code>benchmark.json</code> — policy name, pass or fail, control results, and skips</li>
        <li><code>findings.json</code> — each finding names its engine, probe, severity, and taxonomy</li>
        <li><code>results.sarif</code> — for code scanning in CI</li>
        <li><code>report.html</code> — one file, opened with <code>insidia report --open</code></li>
      </ul>
      <p>Controls map to OWASP LLM, OWASP Agentic, OWASP Web and API, MITRE ATLAS, and CWE where the registry has a mapping. A framework score is the controls that ran, not a percentage we market on this page.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="block">
      <h2>The scanner matrix</h2>
      <p>The same repository holds a permutation matrix of sandboxed targets and planted ground truth. A cell is green only when a scan finds the plant. That matrix is how we decide an engine adapter is done. Coverage pages stay tied to those cells, not to a slide.</p>
      <p><a href="https://github.com/Rushi-Balapure/Insidia-Labs/tree/main/benchmark">Read the benchmark directory</a> · <a href="/#install">Install the CLI</a></p>
    </section>
  </main>
  <Footer />
</Base>
